WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.140 --> 00:00:01.040
- Hey, everyone.

00:00:01.040 --> 00:00:01.940
Welcome to another Coffee Break

00:00:01.940 --> 00:00:03.590
here on my channel, Firm Learning.

00:00:03.590 --> 00:00:04.640
As you know, on my channel,

00:00:04.640 --> 00:00:06.540
I want to help you to become successful

00:00:06.540 --> 00:00:08.620
in the first years of your career.

00:00:08.620 --> 00:00:09.990
So over the last year or so,

00:00:09.990 --> 00:00:11.730
one thing changed for sure.

00:00:11.730 --> 00:00:13.910
And this is that people
spend much more time

00:00:13.910 --> 00:00:15.780
in front of their desk at home

00:00:15.780 --> 00:00:17.870
than they used to in 2019 and before.

00:00:17.870 --> 00:00:19.320
So what does this mean?

00:00:19.320 --> 00:00:22.770
People are wondering, how
do I equip my desk at home

00:00:22.770 --> 00:00:24.220
in the best possible way?

00:00:24.220 --> 00:00:25.260
This was surely a question

00:00:25.260 --> 00:00:27.860
that I asked myself a
lot in the last months.

00:00:27.860 --> 00:00:30.210
So today I wanna show you
how my desk setup looks like

00:00:30.210 --> 00:00:32.870
as a C-level executive
at a German startup,

00:00:32.870 --> 00:00:36.040
and also as a content producer,
of course, for YouTube.

00:00:36.040 --> 00:00:37.480
And as someone who thought a lot

00:00:37.480 --> 00:00:40.760
about how to conduct great
and optimal video conferences.

00:00:40.760 --> 00:00:43.560
So let me show you around here
in my little content room,

00:00:43.560 --> 00:00:45.170
a little paradise here at home,

00:00:45.170 --> 00:00:46.003
and let's do it.

00:00:46.003 --> 00:00:47.360
So the big challenge that I'm facing

00:00:47.360 --> 00:00:48.600
is that we are here in Munich,

00:00:48.600 --> 00:00:50.710
which means apartment
prices are quite high.

00:00:50.710 --> 00:00:53.340
Also, we don't have a huge apartment here.

00:00:53.340 --> 00:00:54.780
So it's limited space.

00:00:54.780 --> 00:00:55.980
We have this little room here

00:00:55.980 --> 00:00:59.020
that I use for content creation
and for work in general.

00:00:59.020 --> 00:01:01.310
Which of course puts me
in a bit of a tough spot,

00:01:01.310 --> 00:01:03.710
that I need to make this multifunctional.

00:01:03.710 --> 00:01:04.695
So here we just have a simple cabinet,

00:01:04.695 --> 00:01:07.000
to store away some stuff.

00:01:07.000 --> 00:01:09.770
What you see here is
my silver play button,

00:01:09.770 --> 00:01:11.420
my Silver YouTube Play Button.

00:01:11.420 --> 00:01:12.690
So for the uninitiated,

00:01:12.690 --> 00:01:16.130
once you pass 100,000
subscribers on YouTube,

00:01:16.130 --> 00:01:20.090
YouTube sends you this
nice little thing here.

00:01:20.090 --> 00:01:21.630
So pretty cool, indeed.

00:01:21.630 --> 00:01:22.820
Quite proud of it, I must say.

00:01:22.820 --> 00:01:24.240
I think the next one that you get

00:01:24.240 --> 00:01:27.160
is only for one million subscribers.

00:01:27.160 --> 00:01:29.000
Then you get a bigger one in gold.

00:01:29.000 --> 00:01:30.490
So still a long way to go.

00:01:30.490 --> 00:01:32.550
Thanks again for everyone who subscribes,

00:01:32.550 --> 00:01:33.900
who supports the channel.

00:01:33.900 --> 00:01:36.150
But now let's maybe
get really to the core,

00:01:36.150 --> 00:01:38.170
to the center of this room.

00:01:38.170 --> 00:01:41.780
And this is of course here, my desk.

00:01:41.780 --> 00:01:44.550
And I will show you all the
individual pieces in a moment,

00:01:44.550 --> 00:01:47.330
go more into detail of all of this.

00:01:47.330 --> 00:01:50.840
Probably the thing that you
will undoubtedly notice here

00:01:50.840 --> 00:01:54.560
are this soundproofing
material at the wall.

00:01:54.560 --> 00:01:55.840
So as you can imagine,

00:01:55.840 --> 00:01:59.460
this took quite a lot of
discussions with my wife,

00:01:59.460 --> 00:02:02.990
for her to allow me to put
all of this here on the wall,

00:02:02.990 --> 00:02:04.370
given that, again,

00:02:04.370 --> 00:02:06.250
we don't have that many
rooms here in the apartment.

00:02:06.250 --> 00:02:08.600
So it's quite a significant
part of the flat.

00:02:08.600 --> 00:02:09.750
The reason that I did there

00:02:09.750 --> 00:02:11.710
is just that the wall
has quite a lot of echo,

00:02:11.710 --> 00:02:14.400
quite a lot of reverb here in the room,

00:02:14.400 --> 00:02:16.430
Which is of course not
great for two reasons:

00:02:16.430 --> 00:02:18.760
first, obviously for creating videos,

00:02:18.760 --> 00:02:21.010
but also in video conferences.

00:02:21.010 --> 00:02:23.671
So I don't know how you feel about it,

00:02:23.671 --> 00:02:24.504
but I always notice it,

00:02:24.504 --> 00:02:26.940
whenever I'm in a video
conference with someone else

00:02:26.940 --> 00:02:29.470
and lots of reverb, lots
of echo in the room,

00:02:29.470 --> 00:02:30.770
really not a great experience,

00:02:30.770 --> 00:02:33.240
especially if you sit
together in a longer meeting.

00:02:33.240 --> 00:02:34.275
So this really helps.

00:02:34.275 --> 00:02:37.810
Frankly, there's still quite
a problem with a reverb

00:02:37.810 --> 00:02:38.790
in this room.

00:02:38.790 --> 00:02:41.120
So this improved it, but not solved it.

00:02:41.120 --> 00:02:43.010
So that's the soundproofing thing.

00:02:43.010 --> 00:02:45.360
Then you, here, of course
see the two lights.

00:02:45.360 --> 00:02:47.120
Again, two things, two purposes.

00:02:47.120 --> 00:02:52.080
I do many videos where I just
sit here in front of my desk,

00:02:52.080 --> 00:02:54.370
and just create a video with a camera

00:02:54.370 --> 00:02:56.450
directly pointed towards me.

00:02:56.450 --> 00:02:57.283
Of course,

00:02:57.283 --> 00:02:58.938
lighting is really one of
the most important things

00:02:58.938 --> 00:03:00.320
when creating videos.

00:03:00.320 --> 00:03:03.000
By the way, most of the
products that I will show you,

00:03:03.000 --> 00:03:05.400
I will include links to them
in the video description.

00:03:05.400 --> 00:03:07.370
So feel free to just check them out,

00:03:07.370 --> 00:03:08.380
if you feel like this is something

00:03:08.380 --> 00:03:09.554
that might be relevant to you as well.

00:03:09.554 --> 00:03:11.460
So we'll show you more in detail

00:03:11.460 --> 00:03:14.180
on what exactly I have here
on my desk in a moment.

00:03:14.180 --> 00:03:15.770
Let me just quickly finish

00:03:15.770 --> 00:03:17.780
by showing you the rest of the room,

00:03:17.780 --> 00:03:20.447
because indeed what you
have here to my left

00:03:20.447 --> 00:03:22.860
is this little cabinet with the TV.

00:03:22.860 --> 00:03:23.693
And then of course,

00:03:23.693 --> 00:03:26.470
lots of room here to stow away things.

00:03:26.470 --> 00:03:28.810
So here you just have
all my audio equipment

00:03:28.810 --> 00:03:30.560
and actually also my gimbal.

00:03:30.560 --> 00:03:33.770
Here you have my old camera
that served me very well

00:03:33.770 --> 00:03:35.680
on my first year on YouTube.

00:03:35.680 --> 00:03:37.713
Here's some additional
lenses for my camera,

00:03:37.713 --> 00:03:41.650
and use some other more
or less gimmicky equipment

00:03:41.650 --> 00:03:42.570
